{title: Praise, My Soul, the King of Heaven}
{artist: Henry F. Lyte / John Goss}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 2/4}
{score: praise-my-soul-the-king-of-heaven.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Praise_My_Soul_The_King_Of_Heaven-Praise_My_Soul-Lauda_Anima)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Praise, my [A7]soul, the [D]King [F#m]of [G]hea[D]ven;
[G]To [D]His [G]feet [A]thy [Bm]tri[Em]bute [A7]bring.
[F#]Ransomed, [Bm]healed, restored, [B7]for[E7]giv[C#7]en,
[F#m]Ev[E7]er[A]more His [Bm]pra[E7]ises [A]sing:
[D]Alle[G]lu[A7]ia! [Bm]Alleluia!
[Bm]Praise the [G]ever[A]lasting [D]King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Praise Him [A7]for His [D]grace [F#m]and [G]fa[D]vor
[G]To [D]our [G]fa[A]thers [Bm]in [Em]dis[A7]tress.
[F#]Praise Him [Bm]still the same [B7]as [E7]ev[C#7]er,
[F#m]Slow [E7]to [A]chide, and [Bm]swift [E7]to [A]bless.
[D]Alle[G]lu[A7]ia! [Bm]Alleluia!
[Bm]Glorious [G]in His [A]faithful[D]ness.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Father [A7]like He [D]tends [F#m]and [G]spares [D]us;
[G]Well [D]our [G]fee[A]ble [Bm]frame [Em]He [A7]knows.
[F#]In His [Bm]hands He gen[B7]tly [E7]bears [C#7]us,
[F#m]Res[E7]cues [A]us from [Bm]all [E7]our [A]foes.
[D]Alle[G]lu[A7]ia! [Bm]Alleluia!
[Bm]Widely [G]yet His [A]mercy [D]flows.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Frail as [A7]summer's [D]flower [F#m]we [G]flour[D]ish,
[G]Blows [D]the [G]wind [A]and [Bm]it [Em]is [A7]gone;
[F#]But while [Bm]mortals rise [B7]and [E7]per[C#7]ish
[F#m]Our [E7]God [A]lives un[Bm]chang[E7]ing [A]on,
[D]Praise Him, [G]Praise [A7]Him, [Bm]Hallelujah
[Bm]Praise the [G]High E[A]ternal [D]One!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Angels, [A7]help us [D]to [F#m]a[G]dore [D]Him;
[G]Ye [D]be[G]hold [A]Him [Bm]face [Em]to [A7]face:
[F#]Sun and [Bm]moon, bow down [B7]be[E7]fore [C#7]Him,
[F#m]Dwell[E7]ers [A]all in [Bm]time [E7]and [A]space.
[D]Alle[G]lu[A7]ia! [Bm]Alleluia!
[Bm]Praise with [G]us the [A]God of [D]grace!
{end_of_verse}
